    "source_anchor": "Fixed PBPS arXiv2609.06905v1 C.1 A3.Ex1 physical4581-4587, A3.Ex2 physical4589-4595, normalized-density differentiation A3.E1 physical4597-4604; authored literal Gaussian posterior-reflection background toward B.13 physical3779-3786.",
    "theorem_delta": "Join actual Gibbs expL1/probability, exported affine normalization and true reflected Gaussian C1 to identify source S_y at every y and its whole compact mean function.",
    "truth_boundary": "ASTIS-authored analytic integration for pinned PBPS2609.06905v1 C.1 actual reflected density A3.Ex1 physical4581-4587, A3.Ex2 4589-4595 and normalized-density differentiation A3.E1 4597-4604; smooth compact core4573-4576 and C.2 physical4654-4664 toward B.13 physical3779-3786. This is not printed standalone theorem. Explicit sufficient-background generalization: finite real Hilbert/Borel E including rank0, C2 V with positive global lower Hessian, eta>0, signed compact C1 f. Original paper also has upper Hessian beta and beta*eta<=1 and smooth compact f. Upper bound and step cap are not needed for this analytic edge; genuine paper consumer retains them. This is attributed background extension, never replacement of B.13 assumptions. Every-y literal source reflected Gibbs law identity and compact mean C1 only; Tf closed-gradient membership, rough L2/H1 B.13, Gamma/halfturn/hypocoercivity, invariance/nonexplosion, implementation error, main theorem, actual-input composition and unbounded expected costs remain separate.",
